WEBVTT

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.270
<b>Inokashira Park</b>

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:18.300
Morning.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:20.300
What's up?

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.300
I don't often see you out here.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.410
I read this.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:25.500
<b>Plan for a New Tokyo 
Inagi Koutaro</b>

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:25.500
Can you sign it?

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.980
Come on, what kind of joke is this?

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:29.710
No, I was seriously impressed.

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:32.430
If a police officer asked for 
an autograph in public,

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.490
it'd cause a problem for you as governor, right?

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:38.240
Signing a book for someone I know 
is a little embarrassing.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:42.750
How's the privatized police 
plan from the book going?

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.130
Everything has to be taken one step at a time.

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:48.740
Many older people dislike change.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.460
Enemies are everywhere.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:54.710
By the way, how are your parents lately?

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:57.450
They're probably fine, wherever they are.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:00.730
I got a letter a while ago saying they 
were going to see the northern lights.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.700
That's just like them.

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:03.700
Bye.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.160
Thank you, Inagi-san!

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:06.870
See you again!

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.490
Enemies everywhere, huh?

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:14.050
<b>To Kuroki Takeru-san 
Tokyo City Governor 
Inagi Koutaro</b>

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.070
<i>In the future,</i>

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:22.610
<i>when something happens beyond 
the normal police's capacity,</i>

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:25.630
<i>they turn to the power of the ACTIVE project.</i>

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:31.820
<i>This is the story of Japan's ACTIVE, 
the Third Mobile Assault Unit.</i>

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:49.100
<b>File 9: Unit 8, Don't Mobilize</b>

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:52.060
Why would I help the governor?

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:53.560
Come on!

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:56.800
Come up with something to make his life easier!

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.490
People don't change.

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.230
No matter what happens,

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:03.320
they ultimately try to return to old systems.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:06.950
I can prove it. You still use Orochi, right?

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.660
Well, yeah, I guess...

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.580
To destroy things they cling to,

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.080
you do things by force and 
be prepared for opposition.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:17.300
Sure you can't come up with 
anything softer, Jirou?

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.090
I'm not Jirou.

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:21.090
My sign is fine.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:22.680
The sign "Mythos."

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.500
What are you talking about?

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:27.630
Aren't you eating here and stuff 
because you're my little brother?

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:29.620
I didn't ask for that.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:30.900
That's fine.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.690
I'll just stay here forever.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:37.750
Then at least get me an Internet connection.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:38.930
What do we do?

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:41.760
It may be a good chance to learn 
about that other matter.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.070
But not here.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.160
Externally, perhaps...

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.040
Yes, this is Hayashida.

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:52.500
Oh, Kuroki-kun is right here.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:56.220
Yesterday at 21:35,

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.880
this Willwear appeared at Hikarigaoka, 
in Nerima Ward.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:03.850
We believe it was after the trade secrets of 
Umeda Electrical Engineering, located here.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:05.470
It escaped?

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:07.930
They surrounded it with helicopters,

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:11.070
but the winds around the building 
kept them from getting close.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.570
Ten minutes later, it used wires

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:16.150
to jump between buildings and escape.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:18.020
Like a spider.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:21.320
That's why local police are calling 
it the "Spider Incident."

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:25.030
It's a "spider" because it's a "spy," right?

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:33.610
Um, what were we talking about?

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:35.030
The Spider Incident.

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:36.380
That's right.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.680
It appears the Willwear was 
listening to conversations

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:40.840
and taking pictures from outside the building.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.170
Talk about old-fashioned.

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.770
It's possible they didn't think to defend

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:47.550
against someone listening in from the outside.

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:50.100
The Willwear model it's based on is foreign.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.850
Foreign?

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:52.680
Yes.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.200
It seems to be using some kind 
of special suction device.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:59.100
I'd love to see how they put it together.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.280
I'd be really happy if we could bring it in!

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:04.230
Is this an urgent matter?

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:05.740
No, the opposite.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.710
There's no need for you to come in for it.

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:10.870
I just thought you'd want to know.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.320
Why?

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:14.080
This is a Willwear case.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.270
Since it's an industrial espionage case,

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:20.420
they're not even sure they'll ask for our help.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.810
But if they do,

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:24.130
we have to be ready to go immediately, right?

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:25.020
That's right.

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:27.220
So I wanted you to be aware, at least.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.050
I see.

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:33.680
Not having Unit 8 involved in the 
investigation stage is a problem.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:35.370
The Tokyo City government

00:05:35.370 --> 00:05:40.220
would like to have an independent unit 
handle all these Willwear cases.

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:42.990
Was this what you were talking 
about when Unit 8 moved

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.240
from the National Police to 
the Metropolitan Police?

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:47.590
That's the best option for Tokyo,

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:50.160
but other municipalities might not like it.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:53.100
At present, we rely on privatized help,

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:56.120
like Sena-kun, but there aren't 
enough people like him.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:05:59.090
Do you know any other former police or

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:02.000
self-defense officers who are 
familiar with Willwears?

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.850
That's a tough question.

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:07.160
We're the first organization of 
our type in the police force.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:08.280
I see.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:10.960
Governor, it's about time.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:13.020
Oh, sorry, Rin.

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:14.680
I'll be back.

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:16.770
A bipartisan faction has found

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:20.080
something else they want to complain 
about with this matter.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.060
Something else?

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:24.430
They want to be rid of 
Tokyo's high-rise buildings.

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:25.440
What?

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:27.610
I understand how they feel.

00:06:28.030 --> 00:06:32.640
Tokyo City's current design was an ad hoc 
reaction to the Quicksand Phenomenon.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:35.120
They think this is a good chance 
to give it a proper design.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:38.010
That's what you're always saying, isn't it?

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:41.010
Hey, I wouldn't say something so extreme.

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:43.800
I do agree it needs redesigned, though.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:46.840
I bet there'd be lots of opposition 
to changing the city's design.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:49.450
There are many opposition movements,

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:51.730
like Showa Town during the monster incident.

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:55.310
But realistically speaking, we must act now.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:59.310
I want to give the city's people 
an ideal they can unite around.

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:01.480
There's more than one ideal, right?

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.990
Politics is about making 
everything into one ideal.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:06.120
You can only have one set of rules.

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.420
I see.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:09.550
So politics is making rules?

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:11.280
You said that before.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:13.280
<b>Conference Room</b>

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:13.990
I'm submitting a proposed ban

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:15.990
on new high-rise construction.

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:19.330
High-rises under construction now 
will be stopped immediately.

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:21.290
Don't be stupid!

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:24.180
Other cities, like Kyoto, have banned

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:27.070
high-rise construction for aesthetic reasons.

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:28.730
Who the hell do you think you are?!

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:29.900
We must best use our space!

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:31.220
You can't do that to private property!

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:34.350
<b>Inagi 
Koutaro</b>

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:34.350
Silence! Silence!

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:36.990
Hey, Sis.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:41.430
How's the investigation into 
Hachijou-senpai going?

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:42.600
Huh?

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:46.530
The ICPO sent a message saying 
that his parents are missing.

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:49.190
It seems he obtained citizenship somewhere.

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:54.450
He used it to come back to Japan, 
so Public Safety is...

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.830
Forget that! Pretend you didn't hear that!

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:00.390
But I did.

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:02.370
You did?

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.780
Sorry, I was kind of spacing out....

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:08.340
There's something I have to ask him.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:12.220
Is there any way I can see him, like I did before?

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:13.600
Before?

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:15.370
At the safe house.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:18.520
Oh, you mean have Shimajirou-kun 
search for him?

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:20.370
What's he doing?

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:24.440
He's helping us with a lot of cases.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:25.540
Oh?

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:26.730
That's surprising.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:33.980
A plan to help the governor?

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:35.460
You're a real slave driver.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:37.070
Don't say that.

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:41.050
So, what's your take on the spider Willwear?

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:44.060
They haven't asked for an 
investigation yet, have they?

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:48.540
But it'll be a nuisance if I have to deal with 
this when I should be helping Inagi-san.

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:52.300
Does the governor even need your help?

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:54.720
Don't talk to your older brother like that.

00:08:55.750 --> 00:09:00.850
If the criminal is a professional industrial 
spy, hire him to draw him out of hiding.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:02.660
A sting, huh?

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:05.100
There are all kinds of restrictions...

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:08.560
An investigative officer doesn't 
need to set the trap.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:13.400
First, I'll see if Bird is behind 
the Willwear incident.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:15.400
Yeah, thanks, Jirou.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:16.610
Mythos.

00:09:21.730 --> 00:09:23.790
The machine specs are a little low,

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:25.300
but I can make it work.

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:27.860
<i>Hello!</i>

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:29.920
<i>What can I do for you?</i>

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:31.420
Let me see...

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:34.880
First, let's see if Spider is 
taking jobs over the net.

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:36.350
I get it.

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:41.470
What the hell are you doing to my dorayaki?!

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:44.890
I'll pay you back later.

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.360
That's not the issue!

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:48.600
And what are you doing in my office?

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:51.710
Jirou here is a civilian cooperator.

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:54.820
Using your computer makes things easier.

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:56.310
What are you talking about?

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.930
Besides, I'm helping you,

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:01.580
but I'm under contract, not a regular 
part of your organization.

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:02.940
Yeah?

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:07.110
Inagi-san said he wanted to do 
something for Tokyo, at least.

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:13.200
The governor's name came up at 
the CEO's meeting I was just at.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:15.590
The construction workers were mad that

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.960
they're starting debate on the new law.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:31.190
<b>Governor Inagi Negotiates With Demonstrators</b>

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:20.530
<i>Can you see this?</i>

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:22.440
<i>People are protesting the ban</i>

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:24.600
<i>on high-rise construction.</i>

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:27.980
<i>A demonstration will be held tomorrow</i>

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:31.190
<i>at Takao Tower, where debate 
on the new law is to begin.</i>

00:10:31.470 --> 00:10:34.650
<i>They're sharing their feelings 
directly with city leaders.</i>

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:34.650
<b>Daitokyo Construction 
Opening the Way to the Future</b>

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:38.160
Politicians don't understand reality at all!

00:10:38.160 --> 00:10:39.370
They don't!

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:43.120
We construction workers made Tokyo what it is!

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:44.370
We made it!

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:46.660
So what do I do now?

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:49.210
You learned how to contact Spider?

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:52.980
He only negotiates directly.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:54.480
He wants us to meet him?

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:56.170
Then you go, Jirou—

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:57.550
Just so we're clear,

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:01.320
he's just an industrial spy who 
has nothing to do with Bird.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:03.590
So I won't help you further.

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:05.820
Okay, you go.

00:11:05.820 --> 00:11:07.940
Our motto is "clean and green."

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:10.590
Ask the other civilian cooperator.

00:11:10.590 --> 00:11:12.250
The other?

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:14.150
Oh, there...

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:21.660
Is that liver with chives?

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:23.870
No, chives with liver.

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:26.160
You're a detective?

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:30.270
The job goes beyond our 
office's ability to handle,

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:32.590
so we'd like you to do it instead.

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:37.460
Your office takes any job?

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.980
No, it depends on payment.

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:41.380
Same here.

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.330
This will be good money.

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:47.600
Even if you don't pay, other people will.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.750
Just so you know, if you do that,

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:52.100
you'll damage your reputation in this industry.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:55.190
It's okay, you don't have to believe me.

00:11:57.120 --> 00:11:59.490
Very well. I'll take the job.

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:01.570
Get the money ready, and wait for my call.

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:06.410
Okay! Gotcha!

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:08.620
Just wait, Spider!

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:18.320
Don't you know the 
"report, inform, consult" rule?

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:20.590
Why did you set a trap on your own?

00:12:20.900 --> 00:12:23.580
You're right...

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:24.750
I'm sorry.

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:27.010
I have another job after this.

00:12:27.270 --> 00:12:28.750
You don't need to worry about it.

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:30.230
Good luck with your work.

00:12:30.230 --> 00:12:32.470
Thank you. Goodbye.

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:40.520
Is the Bali corporation that Spider's 
after also a civilian cooperator?

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:41.920
Well...

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:43.690
They don't know anything.

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:47.120
I just chose them as bait since they were 
a suitable target for an industrial spy.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:49.330
Shimajirou-kun, that's a problem.

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:53.710
Arrest Spider before he steals the secrets,

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:55.670
and there'll be no problem.

00:12:57.350 --> 00:12:58.870
Um, boss,

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:01.380
how about we think of it this way?

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:04.980
A civilian cooperator gave us a tip

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:09.500
that Spider might target a certain company.

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:11.710
In other words, this isn't a sting.

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:13.480
It's a stakeout.

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:15.630
A stakeout, huh?

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:17.660
All right.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:20.940
Kuroki-kun can pay Madoka-chan's 
company directly.

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:23.750
So, when we do go after Spider?

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:24.630
Today.

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:26.010
Then it won't work.

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:29.500
Unit 8 will soon be standing by at Takao Tower.

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:30.960
Standing by?

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:33.460
That demonstration opposing the new law.

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:35.660
Demonstrators showed up in Willwears.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:36.710
Vote "no" on the new law!

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:40.130
<b>Oppose the Law!      Inagi Must Resign      Rise Up, Laborers</b>

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:38.370
Don't take our jobs!

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:40.130
Vote "no" on the new law!

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:43.130
Right now, they're still 
just marching peacefully...

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:45.670
But they're using power-type Willwears,

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:47.510
so everyone's on edge.

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:49.340
Then what about Spider?

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:51.280
Wait until it's over, I guess.

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:53.730
No, that won't be enough time.

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:56.100
If his pattern holds, he'll move fast.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:58.560
I see what Nobujirou-kun is saying, but...

00:13:58.560 --> 00:13:59.520
It's "Jirou."

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:01.230
It isn't "Shimajirou-kun"?

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:03.440
My name is "Mythos."

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:13.950
<b>Governor Inagi Negotiates With Demonstrators</b>

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:07.260
<i>Demonstrators are gathering around 
City Hall, at Takao Tower.</i>

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:12.450
<i>The city Diet planned to discuss the new 
construction law in the afternoon,</i>

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:13.950
<i>but they're still in recess.</i>

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:21.230
All right, thanks.

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:23.670
We don't work for you.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:26.420
I'll buy you dinner, so help us out.

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:29.950
<i>Members of the Diet have returned 
to the meeting hall.</i>

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:33.680
<b>Governor Inagi Negotiates With Demonstrators</b>

00:14:30.310 --> 00:14:33.680
<i>They're very late, but they're 
reconvening the session.</i>

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:37.140
<b>Governor Inagi Negotiates With Demonstrators</b>

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:37.140
<i>Voices of the protesters are getting louder.</i>

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:42.770
But we can't just ignore Spider, can we?

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:45.280
I'm sending Haruka-chan to deal with him.

00:14:45.280 --> 00:14:46.990
Why not me?

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:49.820
The demonstrators' Willwears 
are more powerful than ours.

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:53.280
We need you here.

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:01.580
<b>Requesting</b>

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:02.500
<b>Approved</b>

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:08.710
Deploying stealth mode.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:13.450
This is Oscar III, monitoring the situation.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:17.600
This concludes the pro-ban faction's statement.

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:18.770
Chair, take the vote!

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:21.980
You're ignoring laborer voices to force a vote?

00:15:22.640 --> 00:15:26.280
We're busting into the Diet 
and giving our say directly!

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:29.730
Oscar IV,

00:15:29.730 --> 00:15:32.350
set Koutetsujin Nanakamado Unit.

00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:35.910
Funasaka-san, these are civilians.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:39.120
Please be especially careful 
in using physical force.

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:41.140
Put your own body on the line to stop them.

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:42.140
Understood.

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:45.500
Now you, Kuroki-kun.

00:15:46.410 --> 00:15:47.090
Right!

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:48.800
You get ready, too, Emilia-chan.

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:50.760
Okay, got it!

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:55.110
Boss, a message from Chinju-san, 
Governor Inagi's secretary.

00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:57.770
Tell him we're putting security 
measures in place immediately.

00:15:57.770 --> 00:15:59.060
Well, it's...

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:02.350
We don't need Unit 8 security.

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:03.810
Please don't intervene.

00:16:04.050 --> 00:16:04.770
Huh?

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:06.980
Don't deploy? Why?

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:09.400
The boss is talking to him,

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.200
but they're not granting permission.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.510
Let's go! Follow me!

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:16.740
<i>Demonstrators have started charging forward.</i>

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:17.740
Hey!

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.870
Is the governor... Is Inagi-san saying that?!

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:23.830
Unit 8 is to withdraw immediately.

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:25.500
Please do not intervene.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:27.920
Is that really the governor's order?

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:28.300
Yes.

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:29.940
The governor is

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:33.820
concerned that Unit 8 might collide 
with civilians on the police's behalf.

00:16:34.250 --> 00:16:37.220
People have already complained 
about Unit 9's actions.

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:41.930
If anything happened, it could be a problem 
for the whole Third Mobile Assault Unit.

00:16:41.930 --> 00:16:43.030
That's...

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:44.810
Hey, that's...

00:16:45.030 --> 00:16:47.020
<i>Someone's come out of the building!</i>

00:16:47.490 --> 00:16:48.360
<i>It's the governor!</i>

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:49.570
<i>It's Governor Inagi!</i>

00:16:49.870 --> 00:16:50.700
No!

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:53.780
No. Wait a little longer.

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:55.870
I'm Inagi, the governor of Tokyo.

00:16:56.170 --> 00:16:57.960
I've come here to dispel

00:16:57.960 --> 00:17:01.000
any misunderstandings, and bring 
this to a democratic conclusion.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.650
What do you mean, misunderstandings?

00:17:02.650 --> 00:17:06.400
I intend to oppose the passage of the law

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:08.220
that bans high-rise construction.

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:12.970
But the rules of democratic 
society must be upheld.

00:17:13.230 --> 00:17:15.650
If this is a democracy, you need 
to hear our voices, too!

00:17:15.650 --> 00:17:17.390
We will hear your voices.

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:19.850
<b>Tokyo City, Setagaya Ward</b>

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:19.470
<i>But before that, I want to ask this.</i>

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:22.310
<i>Why are you in your Willwear?</i>

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:22.310
<b>Tokyo City, Machida-shi</b>

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:24.270
<b>Tokyo City, Arakawa Ward</b>

00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:24.270
<i>Is it not an attempt to intimidate?</i>

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:26.350
These are our work clothes!

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:27.350
That's right!

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:28.310
No!

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:33.750
You tried to enter the Diet in those Willwears,

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:35.620
knowing their power full well.

00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:37.290
Then what about Unit 8?

00:17:37.290 --> 00:17:39.030
That's intimidation, isn't it?

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:42.620
<i>There are only normal security guards here.</i>

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:44.140
<i>They're not Unit 8.</i>

00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:47.080
<i>Please! Stay here!</i>

00:17:47.540 --> 00:17:50.670
<i>Or we'll have no choice but to 
tightly regulate Willwears.</i>

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:51.550
Shut up!

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:55.840
You're trying to talk us into 
doing what you want!

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:57.860
Wh-Who are you?

00:17:57.860 --> 00:18:00.030
This is our workplace!

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:02.680
You want to join us?

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:03.680
Then talk to me later!

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:04.800
The opposite!

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:07.270
You guys are a nuisance!

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:08.100
What?

00:18:09.050 --> 00:18:12.570
If regulations on Willwear are 
tightened because of you people,

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:15.670
that will make our jobs harder!

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:19.580
How the hell am I supposed to survive 
without a Willwear at my age?

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:21.020
That's right!

00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:22.520
W-Wait!

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:25.120
We're trying to save our jobs, too.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.550
So that means you can do whatever you want?

00:18:27.550 --> 00:18:29.830
Even cause problems for others?

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:31.020
No, but...

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:32.880
We filled out the paperwork—

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:35.210
End your demonstration immediately!

00:18:35.920 --> 00:18:38.880
Go home! Go home! Go home!

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:40.520
<i>Look at this.</i>

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:42.860
<i>Another group has appeared 
before the demonstrators,</i>

00:18:42.860 --> 00:18:44.060
<i>and is stopping them.</i>

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:46.470
<i>They're both civilians. What is this?</i>

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:51.210
<i>The leader of the demonstrators 
has powered down his Willwear!</i>

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:53.520
<i>He'll speak with Governor Inagi directly.</i>

00:18:53.860 --> 00:18:56.490
They showed up at the perfect time.

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:59.510
I'm glad it appears they'll be able 
to resolve this peacefully.

00:18:59.510 --> 00:19:02.070
This is Oscar III! Spider has appeared!

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:05.240
But my battery's in bad shape...

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:08.210
Oscar III, this is the mobile 
assault command vehicle.

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:11.350
Oscar IV is already on his way.

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:13.710
Send your position and data.

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:14.670
Roger.

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:16.830
Oscar III, sending data.

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:19.620
Transfer complete.

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:21.680
I've gotta change!

00:19:22.290 --> 00:19:25.070
Oscar IV, do you have the information?

00:19:25.070 --> 00:19:27.310
This is Oscar IV. All clear.

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:30.160
Kyoukai-san, I'd like to use my broad-axe.

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:33.560
Your what? You mean the Vibratory Tomahawk?

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:35.930
Yes, the broad-axe.

00:19:35.930 --> 00:19:37.530
It's a tomahawk, isn't it?

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:39.110
That's another word for it.

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:41.740
Funasaka-san's come up with his own name for it...

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:44.830
He's under a lot of stress.

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:48.040
Permission to use the broad-axe granted.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:48.880
Roger!

00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:51.380
Doryuu Broad-axe, set up!

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:56.090
Spider sighted!

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:58.300
Is that Unit 8?

00:19:58.300 --> 00:20:00.840
Change mode two!

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:05.180
I've been waiting for that.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:08.580
Throw!

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:12.930
This is the police. Surrender peacefully.

00:20:12.930 --> 00:20:13.740
Okay!

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:18.560
I... I surrender!

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:21.700
So... Please don't kill me!

00:20:22.100 --> 00:20:24.110
Right, excellent choice.

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:27.830
As you all know, the Third Mobile Assault Unit

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:30.830
cannot cover the entire nation themselves.

00:20:31.090 --> 00:20:32.610
They're doing their best,

00:20:32.610 --> 00:20:35.000
but the country's legal 
structure hasn't caught up.

00:20:35.350 --> 00:20:37.070
That's why,

00:20:37.070 --> 00:20:40.210
in addition to Senars, Inc., 
our first civilian cooperator,

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:43.540
these people have volunteered to be part of the

00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:45.680
volunteer anti-crime organization "Subaru."

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:49.310
As we thank them for their kindness,

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:54.520
I'd like to promise easier access 
to Willwears, and full support

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:56.740
for any volunteers given the

00:20:56.740 --> 00:21:00.480
appropriate authorizations by the Tokyo 
government and Metropolitan Police.

00:21:00.830 --> 00:21:03.110
That volunteer authorization system

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:05.240
was set up really fast, wasn't it?

00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:06.140
Yeah.

00:21:06.140 --> 00:21:10.090
And the sky-rise ban was easily shot down.

00:21:10.090 --> 00:21:12.500
What the hell is the Diet thinking?

00:21:12.840 --> 00:21:14.140
I don't think

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:16.920
that law was ever supposed to pass.

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:17.880
Huh?

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:20.130
So that demonstration was a setup?

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:22.390
Not just the demonstration. The whole thing.

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:24.550
There were three actors involved.

00:21:24.850 --> 00:21:27.180
A Diet member to submit an impossible law,

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:30.850
a Willwear laborer to lead the demonstration,

00:21:31.110 --> 00:21:35.120
and a Willwear user to put together 
a civilian security force.

00:21:35.680 --> 00:21:37.590
These three are different points

00:21:37.590 --> 00:21:40.910
on the same line that someone 
drew, don't you think?

00:21:40.910 --> 00:21:42.470
Is it Hachijou?

00:21:42.470 --> 00:21:43.640
Not just him.

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.810
You asked me to find a way

00:21:46.810 --> 00:21:49.600
to make things easier for the governor, right?

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:53.200
The governor was the one who 
gained the most from this.

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:54.960
What are you trying to say?

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:58.670
That the governor or his secretary set this up.

00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:02.000
Hey, don't talk like that without proof.

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:03.980
When Logos was still functional,

00:22:03.980 --> 00:22:06.630
several things were done 
that I didn't know about.

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:10.020
I thought it was Dog, 
or perhaps the yakuza or mafia,

00:22:10.020 --> 00:22:12.220
but if Bird was working with Inagi...

00:22:12.220 --> 00:22:13.430
Don't say another word!

00:22:15.380 --> 00:22:16.190
Kuroki-san?

00:22:16.890 --> 00:22:19.290
Hinata-chan, what's going on?

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:21.260
Could I talk to you?

00:22:21.260 --> 00:22:21.940
Talk to me?

00:22:23.150 --> 00:22:23.850
Yes.

00:23:54.120 --> 00:23:55.620
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:55.250 --> 00:23:56.820
Ohakonyapachininko.

00:23:56.700 --> 00:24:09.000
File 10: A Farewell Banquet

00:23:57.120 --> 00:24:00.040
Things are starting to seem pretty dark, huh?

00:24:00.040 --> 00:24:03.430
Uncle Funasaka, please help my 
sister with her problems.

00:24:03.430 --> 00:24:05.780
Uncle... I like that.

00:24:05.780 --> 00:24:06.810
Uncle...

00:24:07.110 --> 00:24:07.890
Uncle?

00:24:07.890 --> 00:24:08.470
Ah!
